Host unit tests
===============

From firmware/:

    ~/.platformio/penv/bin/pio test -e native

Requires a host C++ compiler and PlatformIO. The first run downloads the native
platform and Unity. No board, Arduino SDK, credentials or serial port is needed.
The same command runs in the firmware GitHub Actions workflow; embedded
firmware and experiment builds remain a separate job. To run only the e-paper
suite, add `-f test_epaper`.

The native environment compiles production text.cpp, generated fonts and
recording.cpp. test_text uses the existing tools/preview/Seeed_GFX.h framebuffer
stub. test_recording replaces only esp_heap_caps.h with malloc/free and a switch
for allocation failure. test_epaper compiles the real sticky/epaper.h driver
against a small fake controller bus in test/support, sharing the same allocator.
Those include paths belong only to the native build.

Coverage:
- UTF-8 decoding/recovery, copy boundaries, glyph support and fallback;
- wrapping, explicit newlines, narrow boxes, truncation and drawing placement;
- streaming WAV header bytes, publishing samples, capacity, duration, reuse,
  reallocation, allocation failure and cleanup;
- e-paper shadow priming, both RAM planes, polarity, row stride and successive
  partial updates, in both directions at the icon and the two RAM boundaries.

These tests do not validate the physical display, PSRAM, task scheduling,
concurrent memory visibility, GPIO, microphone or network. No hardware tests
or device flashing are part of this suite. Add tests for readily isolated logic;
do not duplicate production algorithms in test substitutes.
